   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Hello Phil,</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Is it possible to assign items to specific factors (in a\r\nbifactor model) using item labels only, without any reference to their order?\r\nThe regular method as below is based on the item orders.  </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(0,112,192)\">specific &lt;- c</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,112,192)\">(1,1,2,1,2,1,2,1,1,1,2,1,2,1)</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Best</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Afshin </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\"> </span></p></div></div><div><div><br></div><span class=\"gmail_signature_prefix\">-- </span><br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Afshin Khosravi, PhD TEFL, MA TEFL, <div><div><div><br><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "51Dm3v6aAwAJ",
   "from": "Phil Chalmers",
   "author": "b330c2028fed415b",
   "date": "2024-07-09T19:14:17Z",
   "subject": "Re: Assigning item with labels",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">It certainly could be possible to do this. Could you give an example of what would be more convenient for you to work with? This approach is generally a shorthand, but I agree it&#39;s somewhat suboptimal. I&#39;m currently thinking something like <div><br></div><div>spec &lt;- &quot;S1 = 1,2,4,...</div><div>              S2 = 3,5,...&quot;<br><div><br clear=\"all\"><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Thu, Sep 28, 2023 at 12:45 PM Afshin Khosravi &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">afshinkho...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Hello Phil,</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\">Is it possible to assign items to specific factors (in a\r\nbifactor model) using item labels only, without any reference to their order?\r\nThe regular method as below is based on the item orders.  </span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:rgb(0,112,192)\">specific &lt;- c</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,112,192)\">(1,1,2,1,2,1,2,1,1,1,2,1,2,1)</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Best</span><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:&quot;Times New Roman&quot;,&quot;serif&quot;\"></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 0.0001pt;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;font-family:Arial,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Afshin </span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin:0cm 0cm 8pt;line-height:107%;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><span style=\"font-size:12pt;line-height:107%\"> </span></p></div></div><div><div><br></div><span class=\"gmail_signature_prefix\">-- </span><br><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Afshin Khosravi, PhD TEFL, MA TEFL, <div><div><div><br><div><br></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
