   "date": "2024-07-09T19:26:08Z",
   "subject": "Re: Assigning item with labels",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">This is something that&#39;s passed to the mirt.model() builder, so when implemented you could use item names too. So this:<div><br></div><div> specific &lt;- &quot;S1 = 7,9,10,11,13,15,17,18,21,22,24,27,31<br>              S2 = 1,3,6,8,16,29,32<br>              S3 = 2,4,5,12,14,19,20,23,25,26,28,30&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>could also be specified as </div><div><br></div><div> specific &lt;- &quot;S1 = item7, item9,...<br>              S2 = item1,item3,...<br>              S3 = item2, item4, ...&quot;</div><div><br></div><div>It&#39;s just a matter of preference. </div><div><br><div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Phil</div></div></div></div><br></div></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_attr\">On Tue, Jul 9, 2024 at 3:21 PM Afshin Khosravi &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">afshinkho...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Thank you Phil. I think you are again referring to item order. I want item labels. Like &#39;ME12F&#39;, &#39;SE156G&#39;, etc. </div><div>Afshin</div></div></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
